# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Environment and secrets
.env

# Local data: answer images are sensitive and must never be committed
data/storage/
data/*.db
data/samples/*.png

# Node
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Handwriting samples: real people's writing, never committed.
#
# The exam *definition* (question paper, answer key, seed_exam.json) is tracked
# and has to be - the application seeds its rubrics from it at startup. What is
# excluded is the collected handwriting itself: the scanned booklets and the
# page images and transcripts derived from them.
#
# This means the 2.9% character error rate in the README cannot be reproduced
# from a fresh clone. That is a deliberate trade: the writers are identifiable
# from their handwriting, and a public repository is the wrong place for it.
# The benchmark report in data/benchmarks/ records the result; to re-run it, get
# the booklets from the team.
data/exam/scans/
data/exam/pages/

# Generated datasets and benchmark reports (large, reproducible from scripts)
data/synthetic*/
data/synthetic_pilot/
data/train/
data/benchmarks/
models/
data/*.zip
# A zip written without an extension by an interrupted command leaves 38 MB of
# dataset in data/ that the pattern above does not catch.
data/zia*

# The generated project report and its figures.
#
# The report is rebuilt from the repository with:
#     .venv\Scripts\python scripts\report\figures.py
#     .venv\Scripts\python scripts\report\build_report.py
#     powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts\report\finalise.ps1
#
# The figures are excluded for the same reason data/exam/pages is: one of them
# (fig_4_7_segmentation.png) shows a real answer page, and the volunteers who
# wrote those pages are identifiable from their handwriting. The .docx and .pdf
# embed that figure, so they are excluded too. The measurements the report
# quotes are kept, because they are numbers rather than images and the report's
# claims should be checkable.
docs/report/figures/
docs/report/assets/
docs/report/*.docx
docs/report/*.pdf
